Arduino Line Following Robot

This is a line-following robot project that I built using an Arduino Uno.

This project was developed collaboratively with Esma Çelik.

The robot uses three IR sensors to detect the position of the line. Based on the sensor readings, the Arduino controls two DC motors to move forward, turn left, turn right, or stop.

Components

* Arduino Uno R3
* L298N Motor Driver
* 3-channel IR Sensor
* 2 DC Motors
* Robot Chassis
* Wheels
* Battery Holder
* Jumper Wires

How It Works

The three IR sensors are placed at the front of the robot.

The Arduino reads the sensor values and decides which direction the robot should move.

* Center sensor detects the line → Robot moves forward
* Left sensor detects the line → Robot turns left
* Right sensor detects the line → Robot turns right

The L298N motor driver controls the direction and speed of the motors.

Software

The robot was programmed using the Arduino IDE with C/C++.

